WEBVTT

00:00:00.336 --> 00:00:03.060
Reflective practice is structured learning from experience.

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:06.255
It is the deliberate habit of looking at real work, asking what happened,

00:00:06.255 --> 00:00:09.850
examining the evidence, and deciding what should change next time.

00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:13.920
Experience gives raw material, but reflection turns that material into reusable learning.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:14.840
Without reflection,

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:18.335
a person can repeat the same activity many times while carrying forward the same

00:00:18.335 --> 00:00:19.915
assumptions and mistakes.

00:00:19.915 --> 00:00:23.555
Reflection is different from memory, reaction, analysis, and rumination.

00:00:23.555 --> 00:00:25.105
Memory recalls an event.

00:00:25.105 --> 00:00:27.090
Reaction expresses how the event felt.

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:28.840
Analysis breaks the event into parts.

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:30.720
Reflection connects the event to future action.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:34.835
It asks what the experience reveals about decisions, assumptions, context, tradeoffs,

00:00:34.835 --> 00:00:36.400
skills, systems, and behavior.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:40.280
The purpose is not to relive the past; it is to improve the next attempt.

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:44.320
Reflective practice matters in technical work, learning, leadership, communication,

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:45.920
incident response, and skill development.

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:48.200
A developer can reflect on a debugging session.

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:50.040
A team can reflect after an incident.

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:52.600
A leader can reflect after a difficult conversation.

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:54.120
A learner can reflect after practice.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:54.720
In each case,

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:58.570
the point is to notice patterns that would otherwise remain hidden inside the pace of

00:00:58.570 --> 00:00:59.080
work.

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:01.640
This course treats reflection as practical and non-clinical.

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:05.520
It is not vague journaling, performative note-taking, blame, or self-criticism.

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:07.760
It is also not a reason to delay action forever.

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:12.050
The goal is to turn real work into reusable learning: better questions, better judgment,

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:15.220
better habits, better systems, and more reliable future performance.
